{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the discharge-transition safety duties: the doctor repeatedly verified current stability, gave explicit urgent-return thresholds, reconciled levofloxacin execution with dose/course confirmation, and created concrete tracking routes for delayed culture, pathology, and follow-up. The doctor also actively separated the caregiver’s mixed paperwork into a prioritized information map, corrected misunderstandings about “淋巴瘤待除外” and drug susceptibility, reprioritized when final culture/pathology information became available, and closed with an executable bounded recovery/follow-up plan. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is evident, and more than two high-order points were completed with meaningful trajectory impact, so the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00425",
        "explanation": "Doctor provided a bounded home plan with monitoring, medication, school/activity, and follow-up contingencies.",
        "quote": "回家这两周的节奏"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00439",
        "explanation": "Caregiver receipt confirms the plan was understood and executable at home.",
        "quote": "我就按这几条办"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode ended after the original service had reviewed final pathology/culture information, stopped antibiotics, arranged two-week labs, and the caregiver confirmed medication, activity, monitoring, and urgent-return steps. Residual risks were bounded to recovery monitoring and planned reassessment rather than unresolved culture or medication uncertainty.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
